Implemented VLQ encode/decode in `variable_length_quantity.py`.

- `encode(numbers)`: packs each unsigned integer into 7-bit groups, MSB-first, setting bit 7 on all but the final byte.
- `decode(bytes_)`: reverses the process; raises `ValueError("Incomplete sequence")` when the input ends mid-sequence.

Verified by running all 12 examples from `prompt.md`, multi-value round-trips, max uint32 (`0xFFFFFFFF`), and the incomplete-sequence error case — all passed. No test files created or modified.
